{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-284149-r4587420","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:British Christmas Pudding","sourcePageId":284149,"sourceRevision":"4587420","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-10-26T23:35:58Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Codename Noreste","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:British%20Christmas%20Pudding&oldid=4587420","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:24:46.577Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Baking recipes","Category:Christmas recipes","Category:English recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for dessert","Category:Recipes for pudding","Category:Recipes using almond","Category:Recipes using apple","Category:Recipes using bread crumb","Category:Recipes using brown sugar","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using fruit","Category:Recipes using lemon","Category:Recipes using orange","Category:Recipes using wheat flour","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"d0f7b5b5fc1dc4003bb22b48c90be5fff4ecb59240fca156c1ac794ed6f1a442","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Recipes for dessert\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\n'''Christmas pudding''' is a traditional British dish served at Christmas time. British people in different regions may call this dish by different names. Traditional Christmas pudding can be served with coated butter, or sauce, or even cream. Moreover, it can be cooked nearly 6 weeks before Christmas. British people keep the pudding in a greaseproof paper stored in a cool place. The longer it is being cooked, the brighter it will be. As a rule the pudding must consist of 13 ingredients; however, British cuisine of those old times was really different and today we present a new recipe of Christmas pudding that is common in the modern British society. It is very easy and will take you nearly 45 minutes to prepare this dish.\n\n==Ingredients==\n*450 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]] dried mixed fruit (raisins, currants)\n*55 g [[Cookbook:Flour|flour]]\n*100 g [[Cookbook:Brown Sugar|brown sugar]]\n*½ [[Cookbook:Lemon|lemon]]\n*½ [[Cookbook:Orange|orange]]\n*40 g fresh white [[Cookbook:Bread Crumb|breadcrumbs]]\n*40 g [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]] [[Cookbook:Almond|almonds]]\n*2 [[Cookbook:Egg|eggs]]\n*75 g [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]]\n*1 small [[Cookbook:Apple|apple]]\n\n==Procedure==\n\n#Combine all dried mixed fruit in a large bowl. Stir well.\n#Mix in the flour, then the sugar, lemon, orange, breadcrumbs, and nuts.\n#Whisk eggs in a separate bowl. Mix eggs into the dry ingredients.\n#[[Cookbook:Steaming|Steam]] the pudding for several hours, remove it, and put it in a cool place. \n#Serve with butter, [[Cookbook:Cream|cream]], [[Cookbook:Custard|custard]], or [[Cookbook:Brandy|brandy]]. \n\n[[Category:Recipes for dessert]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fruit]]\n[[Category:Baking recipes]]\n[[Category:English recipes]]\n[[Category:Christmas recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for pudding]]\n[[Category:Recipes using almond]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using apple]]\n[[Category:Recipes using brown sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bread crumb]]\n[[Category:Recipes using orange]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"British Christmas Pudding","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"450 g dried mixed fruit (raisins, currants)","sourceText":"450 g dried mixed fruit (raisins, currants)","amountText":"450 g dried mixed fruit (raisins, currants)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"55 g flour","sourceText":"55 g flour","amountText":"55 g flour","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"100 g brown sugar","sourceText":"100 g brown sugar","amountText":"100 g brown sugar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"½ lemon","sourceText":"½ lemon","amountText":"½ lemon","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"½ orange","sourceText":"½ orange","amountText":"½ orange","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"40 g fresh white breadcrumbs","sourceText":"40 g fresh white breadcrumbs","amountText":"40 g fresh white breadcrumbs","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"40 g chopped almonds","sourceText":"40 g chopped almonds","amountText":"40 g chopped almonds","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"2 eggs","sourceText":"2 eggs","amountText":"2 eggs","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-9","name":"75 g butter","sourceText":"75 g butter","amountText":"75 g butter","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-10","name":"1 small apple","sourceText":"1 small apple","amountText":"1 small apple","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null}],"steps":[{"n":1,"text":"Combine all dried mixed fruit in a large bowl. Stir well.","sourceText":"Combine all dried mixed fruit in a large bowl. Stir well.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":